1
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:23,700
 Stars, galaxy, in astral seas abound, on cosmic paths we'll trace.

2
00:00:24,000 --> 00:01:33,010
 Man, her wing is such a wandering thing.

3
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:40,100
 Behind us all, come see, come take your place.

4
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:55,430
 We're leaving soon for...

5
00:01:55,430 --> 00:02:08,710
 Decision, no. Surrender, ultimatum, no more, no more.

6
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,830
 What is in Colonel Pierre's report, and the report of the commander,

7
00:02:14,330 --> 00:02:18,780
 and those of our agents on Cassiopeia, all agree we have no chance at all.

8
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:20,290
 Not one chance in a million.

9
00:02:20,810 --> 00:02:23,190
 Gentlemen, this must be made crystal clear.

10
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:24,850
 We have virtually no chance.

11
00:02:24,990 --> 00:02:25,910
 What is to be our decision?

12
00:02:26,190 --> 00:02:29,300
 First, I trust we are all resolutely agreed not to cede Yama.

13
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,450
 I propose we vote by raising of hands.

14
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:38,610
 Our status is special.

15
00:02:38,750 --> 00:02:43,570
 We are located too far away for our ships to arrive in sufficient time to be useful in combat.

16
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:46,090
 Therefore, I will respectfully abstain.

17
00:02:46,090 --> 00:02:52,710
 For us, I may assure the Council, forces from the constellation of Scorpio are already on their way.

18
00:02:53,280 --> 00:02:56,750
 I believe that our 20 large warships will arrive in time.

19
00:02:57,610 --> 00:02:59,050
 Two are on their way.

20
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:03,230
 Ten battlecruisers, six frigates, ten ultrafighters.

21
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:06,330
 I am very sorry, but we are also too far away.

22
00:03:06,390 --> 00:03:07,390
 Our ships are en route.

23
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:10,110
 Perhaps if the combat goes on long enough, then...

24
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:11,630
 Ours have already left, Brigale.

25
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:13,450
 They will certainly arrive in time.

26
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:15,890
 Sixteen ships to the line and their escort vessels.

27
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:19,970
 Ours are coming. I have received confirmation of it.

28
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:22,250
 Our fleet will be here very soon.

29
00:03:23,110 --> 00:03:25,490
 At least fourteen large combat vessels.

30
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:29,710
 You can count on ours twelve battleships.

31
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:31,330
 Thank you, gentlemen.

32
00:03:32,450 --> 00:03:36,010
 I knew that the Confederation could count on your loyalty to our cause.

33
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:40,930
 Earth has also confirmed it will carry out its duty.

34
00:03:42,310 --> 00:03:45,530
 And whom do you wish to designate as Commander-in-Chief of this force?

35
00:03:46,750 --> 00:03:50,560
 Colonel Gare continues to command our complete confidence.

36
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:54,350
 I believe I speak for all of us. He is well qualified to assume command.

37
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:55,430
 Thank you, gentlemen.

38
00:03:55,430 --> 00:04:00,270
 We will then have the mightiest space fleet ever assembled in living memory of mankind.

39
00:04:00,550 --> 00:04:03,430
 Consider, with all of the Omega ships, as well as those of Earth,

40
00:04:03,650 --> 00:04:06,270
 we will put forth more than 100 combat ships.

41
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:11,610
 But this flotilla, compared to Yama's strength, is insufficient to meet and repel that superior force.

42
00:04:11,930 --> 00:04:15,970
 Gentlemen, should we risk our ships and all our men in useless combat?

43
00:04:16,470 --> 00:04:18,220
 Colonel, how can you ask that question?

44
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:22,180
 Colonel, we are aware that you agreed, however it concerns human dignity.

45
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:24,390
 Even if we have no chance of winning,

46
00:04:24,670 --> 00:04:29,070
 even if we must go to our own destruction for the honor and dignity of men, we must fight.

47
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:32,450
 Precisely what I had hoped you would say. Thank you all.

48
00:04:32,450 --> 00:04:38,080
 There must be some sort of plan that we can devise, one that might give us a chance.

49
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:41,680
 Our young officers, didn't they come up with a plan that was effective?

50
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:46,050
 Yes, our children did succeed in an exploit that was miraculous,

51
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:48,170
 but we can't count on its working again.

52
00:04:49,110 --> 00:04:50,730
 And as for a plan, on this occasion,

53
00:04:50,870 --> 00:04:55,610
 I think I must call upon our eminent strategist, Professor Maestro.

54
00:04:55,850 --> 00:04:56,240
 Maestro?

55
00:04:57,780 --> 00:05:00,980
 Yes, yes, we must keep two considerations in mind,

56
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:03,880
 the two factors that make the forces of Yam so overwhelming.

57
00:05:04,610 --> 00:05:07,010
 First, the terrible power of their weapons,

58
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:09,050
 and there, we can do nothing.

59
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:12,750
 Yes, we could enhance our own protection capability,

60
00:05:12,910 --> 00:05:14,650
 but time is short and it's too late for that.

61
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:17,310
 Second, what makes them invulnerable

62
00:05:17,310 --> 00:05:19,410
 is the power of their own protection shield,

63
00:05:19,510 --> 00:05:21,550
 the subnucleonic field of force

64
00:05:21,550 --> 00:05:23,530
 which reacts on the structure of matter itself.

65
00:05:23,630 --> 00:05:25,130
 Not one of our craft could get through it.

66
00:05:25,170 --> 00:05:26,910
 No ray or explosion can penetrate it.

67
00:05:27,210 --> 00:05:28,770
 Even gamma rays are deflected.

68
00:05:29,030 --> 00:05:31,190
 And so I will try to discover a means

69
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,530
 of altering the continuity

70
00:05:32,530 --> 00:05:34,690
 of their devilishly clever field of force.

71
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:36,570
 And if I find a theoretical solution,

72
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:38,150
 we may find a way of winning.

73
00:05:38,350 --> 00:05:40,220
 Only it's not by any means, sure.

74
00:05:41,790 --> 00:05:46,320
 We could also try by ultrasonic beams directing them at the brain circuits,

75
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:49,980
 hoping to deregulate the programming and to render the creatures useless,

76
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:54,030
 but I hasten to point out that the distances in questions, well, I don't know.

77
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:56,400
 All that is hardly reassuring, Professor.

78
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,000
 I know, I know, I agree, I agree.

79
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:00,380
 I think we are looking in the wrong place.

80
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:04,100
 This whole conflict seems rooted in materialistic considerations.

81
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:07,020
 In the universe, there are other forces than material.

82
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,420
 Why shouldn't we seek them out and ally ourselves with them?

83
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:13,580
 What are you talking about? What are the forces?

84
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:16,740
 Forces that no one can define or really describe.

85
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:21,280
 Those which make a man worthy of the name seek justice and beauty and joy.

86
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,500
 Professor, you are living in fantasy.

87
00:06:25,850 --> 00:06:27,610
 A rogue professor's lost his reason.

88
00:06:27,750 --> 00:06:29,890
 No, I assure you, you haven't understood.

89
00:06:30,010 --> 00:06:31,670
 You don't understand at all what I'm talking about.

90
00:06:31,730 --> 00:06:32,490
 Never mind, it doesn't matter.

91
00:06:33,010 --> 00:06:36,290
 I shall go now and follow my thoughts in the matter and so forth.

92
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,500
 My nose!

93
00:06:57,800 --> 00:07:46,580
 Jam their radar and interfere with their communication, here's what we'll do.

94
00:07:46,580 --> 00:08:19,810
 There are too many preparations that would have to be carried out in your plan.

95
00:08:19,810 --> 00:08:22,830
 And besides, they've learned from their earlier experience.

96
00:08:22,830 --> 00:08:25,990
 No, the Yamagais, they'll be on their guard.

97
00:08:25,990 --> 00:08:29,590
 My idea is a lot simpler, listen.

98
00:08:29,590 --> 00:08:31,590
 In order to get into the city, we'll promise them anything.

99
00:08:31,590 --> 00:08:33,830
 Anything they want to know.

100
00:08:33,830 --> 00:08:38,340
 Strategy of attack, details of the confederation secret meetings, anything.

101
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:40,500
 Because we're in a war to the death.

102
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,500
 And it's our intelligence against their physical force.

103
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,130
 In the end, they are only machines.

104
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:47,360
 Once inside, Psyche, Metro, and I will know what to do.

105
00:08:53,310 --> 00:08:58,620
 This time, no half measures.

106
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:00,760
 It all blows up, ammunition and computer.

107
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:03,810
 Nice plan, but first we have to get inside.

108
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:07,110
 And it seems to me in your calculations, you've overlooked one detail.

109
00:09:07,410 --> 00:09:08,410
 How do we get out again?

110
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:11,780
 It's not important whether we get out or not, Metro.

111
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:13,420
 What is important is we succeed.

112
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:17,100
 Once the central circuits of the great computer are destroyed, we've won.

113
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:18,820
 Isn't that worth taking the risk?

114
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,180
 Because the alternative is unthinkable.

115
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,140
 Oh, well, why didn't you say so in the first place?

116
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:24,200
 It's quite a good plan.

117
00:09:25,010 --> 00:09:27,170
 Yes, if you manage to get in, it's a good plan.

118
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:30,160
 The only drawback is that it's a suicide mission.

119
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:31,100
 What does Psyche think?

120
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:36,950
 If there is a chance of success, even a very slim one, shouldn't we take it?

121
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:41,340
 For the time being, we had better wait until Maestro tells us his plan.

122
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:44,400
 Strategically speaking, Piero's plan is excellent.

123
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:46,740
 Tactically, I don't see any chance of it working.

124
00:09:47,390 --> 00:09:51,330
 It's no worse odds than we'd have trying to attack Yama, even with all our ships.

125
00:09:52,010 --> 00:09:53,880
 Where is all this going to end?

126
00:09:54,450 --> 00:09:56,620
 The world going to disappear?

127
00:09:58,430 --> 00:10:03,170
 It's our lives, if we must.

128
00:10:03,170 --> 00:10:05,470
 We can accept that.

129
00:10:06,030 --> 00:10:07,500
 The lives of our children.

130
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:12,090
 Now, the cyanetic energy, the mass of a given body.

131
00:10:12,230 --> 00:10:13,190
 No, no, no, that's not it.

132
00:10:13,510 --> 00:10:17,110
 Well, Maestro, still stewing in your prehistoric arithmetic, I would do it faster.

133
00:10:17,290 --> 00:10:18,850
 I'll start again. Out of my way.

134
00:10:19,050 --> 00:10:20,530
 Oh, it would be easy for me.

135
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:24,280
 Oh, would it? Now, now, now, you take yourself for the great computer, I suppose.

136
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:26,040
 Perhaps I do. Perhaps I don't.

137
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:28,220
 Aren't you taking yourself for the great Einstein?

138
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:35,260
 Yes, I see. You may be right.

139
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:38,900
 I'll try that line of thought. Where's that leading us?

140
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:43,880
 No, no, no, that formula won't work. Try another one.

141
00:10:52,250 --> 00:11:01,620
 my father really wasn't too crazy about my plan psyche listen I'm going to try

142
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:05,740
 to carry out the mission even if it means define his authority you with me if

143
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:10,160
 there's the slightest chance of saving our universe yes I will go with you pure

144
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:15,190
 you know that never let you go off on such a mission knowing that you might

145
00:11:15,190 --> 00:11:34,100
 not return you who knows we just might have a chance oh no no you've got it

146
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:39,360
 won't work may I recall to you the theory of dynamic geometry topological

147
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:42,600
 wormholes in the structure of space allow physical bodies to be displaced

148
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,910
 from one point to another.

149
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:45,690
 - No, no, not at all, Metro.

150
00:11:45,690 --> 00:11:48,190
 You're applying that old outdated theory of Wheeler,

151
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:50,260
 which in any case can't be applied in this case.

152
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:52,410
 If in confronting the protection shield,

153
00:11:52,410 --> 00:11:54,230
 we don't reconstitute the continuum of matter,

154
00:11:54,230 --> 00:11:55,530
 nothing is going to get past it.

155
00:11:55,530 --> 00:11:57,890
 Neither spacecraft, nor projectile, nor ultrasound,

156
00:11:57,890 --> 00:12:00,330
 nor anything else in the universe.

157
00:12:00,330 --> 00:12:04,480
 Leave me alone now, I want to be alone to think.

158
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:07,530
 - Ah, these humans, I really do not understand.

159
00:12:07,530 --> 00:12:09,530
 There is no point in spraining your circuits

160
00:12:09,530 --> 00:12:11,740
 to try to help them, I never learn.

161
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:13,310
 - Yes, Maestro.

162
00:12:13,310 --> 00:12:15,710
 - I do not wish to be disturbed for anything.

163
00:12:15,710 --> 00:12:17,970
 Is that understood? You will not disturb me.

164
00:12:46,510 --> 00:12:48,860
 That's about right for the geometry. That should do it.

165
00:12:50,450 --> 00:12:54,280
 The same, there are other values that he forces.

166
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:15,880
 See, if we cut engines and coast right up to the Howard Star just missing it, we get in behind them.

167
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:18,200
 By the time they realize it, it will inflict large losses.

168
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,760
 Howard Star, watch it, Pierre. It's unstable.

169
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:22,250
 Yes, I know that it is.

170
00:13:22,410 --> 00:13:25,870
 Colonel, unidentified flying object entering our field. Come quickly.

171
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:33,460
 It will pass us very close.

172
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:38,560
 It can't be from Yama. It's coming from the opposite direction, and it reflects just one radar signal.

173
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:42,020
 It can't be them. It doesn't concern us. We have other fish to fry.

174
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:45,980
 The fleet from Aldebaran announces its arrival. Request permission to land.

175
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:47,910
 Permission to land granted.

176
00:13:49,680 --> 00:14:08,620
 Aldebaran fleet approaching. Land on Omega granted.

177
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:23,970
 Must we die already?

178
00:14:24,870 --> 00:14:27,180
 I'd look forward to so much more life.

179
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:32,180
 Faith. The forces of evil must not triumph.

180
00:14:32,950 --> 00:14:36,270
 What are we to do? We are so weak, so defenseless.

181
00:14:36,270 --> 00:14:43,800
 Physical force is not all. Have confidence. We will tell you what to do when the time comes. Sleep in peace.

182
00:14:57,130 --> 00:15:05,030
 Just received a message from the forces of Yama. We are sending it through to you now.

183
00:15:06,810 --> 00:15:14,620
 Your efforts to resist us are useless. In 24 hours, our forces will be at your perimeter. That will be your last chance to surrender.

184
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,460
 Do not force us to make you suffer the same fate as Cassiopeia.

185
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:19,430
 Yes?

186
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:22,960
 Colonel, the Earth ships are now approaching.

187
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:25,610
 Yes? And those of Hydra?

188
00:15:25,970 --> 00:15:27,330
 They just radioed, Colonel.

189
00:15:27,330 --> 00:15:31,180
 Very well. Instruct them not to land. They are to stay in orbit now.

190
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:33,820
 There is no time to receive their delegation.

191
00:15:34,190 --> 00:15:36,650
 Well, enough speculation. Now we'll have to take action.

192
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:38,780
 Mass all the fleets in formation.

193
00:15:39,590 --> 00:15:42,110
 I'll go activate the program to get them into the air.

194
00:15:42,530 --> 00:15:47,260
 By zero four hours, they should be aloft and join with the ones that are waiting there already.

195
00:15:47,630 --> 00:15:51,320
 That's fine. Call Maestro. It's urgent.

196
00:15:52,350 --> 00:15:53,380
 I see. He should be here.

197
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:56,300
 Colonel, the professor requested he not be disturbed.

198
00:15:56,610 --> 00:16:00,540
 What? Time like this? I think he's gone crazy.

199
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:12,140
 Here again, safe and sound.

200
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:14,660
 What a magnificent Star Trek I had.

201
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:17,800
 Well, now, what do you bring us, Colonel? Good news.

202
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:19,540
 Let's go, man. The fleet is ready.

203
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:24,150
 Maestro, we're about to leave. This is not the time to sit and dream.

204
00:16:24,510 --> 00:16:26,560
 Ah, no, friend, you don't understand.

205
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:28,880
 I went away to reassure myself about our destiny.

206
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:31,360
 Our fight was entirely materialistic.

207
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,400
 We would have lost it to a materialism more powerful than ours.

208
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:37,480
 But there exists in the universe not only the materialistic.

209
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:40,480
 Now I know that. We aren't alone in space.

210
00:16:41,150 --> 00:16:42,990
 Children, now we must part.

211
00:16:43,360 --> 00:16:44,770
 I know that duty calls you.

212
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:51,020
 But seeing you all go just like that, all three of you without me, it's very hard to bear.

213
00:16:51,290 --> 00:16:54,110
 It is more difficult for you who remain behind.

214
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:58,390
 We are caught up in the action of battle with no time to reflect on them.

215
00:16:58,590 --> 00:17:00,380
 You mustn't worry. I'll be busy here.

216
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:02,890
 Now, my dear, time to go.

217
00:17:04,010 --> 00:17:15,280
 Cry. Now it's your turn.

218
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:20,210
 I never told you before, only now that I may never see you again.

219
00:17:20,650 --> 00:17:22,380
 Hero, I want you to know this.

220
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:26,580
 Your father and I are very, very proud of you.

221
00:17:30,590 --> 00:17:31,930
 Men.

222
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:43,030
 Captain.

223
00:17:44,450 --> 00:17:45,190
 Yes, Colonel?

224
00:17:45,810 --> 00:17:48,840
 Concerning your plan for an attack, no initiatives.

225
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:50,290
 You will await my orders.

226
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:51,490
 Yes, Colonel.

227
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:06,120
 Even at a time like this, we're not allowed to be an ordinary couple.

228
00:18:13,670 --> 00:18:14,870
 This is Colonel Pierre.

229
00:18:15,690 --> 00:18:16,610
 To all units.

230
00:18:17,210 --> 00:18:20,990
 To all units, to all crew members of the Omega Confederation.

231
00:18:21,470 --> 00:18:23,990
 To all units of the Omega Confederation.

232
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:43,090
 You're still going to do what you said you would?

233
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:49,140
 I tend to think it's the first time you've ever commanded such a fine ship.

234
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:51,360
 I admit it's a shame to have to sacrifice it.

235
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:52,320
 It really is a shame.

236
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:55,970
 For whatever fate has in store, here we go.

237
00:18:56,090 --> 00:18:59,270
 I'll leave the formation right now, and then we're on our way.

238
00:18:59,580 --> 00:19:00,810
 No, wait, Piero.

239
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:03,000
 Wait for what? It's now or never.

240
00:19:03,290 --> 00:19:06,430
 Please, wait just a little. I ask you not to do it yet.

241
00:19:13,530 --> 00:19:20,200
 Very soon, we will have a practical demonstration of whether your new ships are resistant.

242
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,930
 We might. Then again, we might not.

243
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:25,690
 Unidentified object detected on radar screen.

244
00:19:26,010 --> 00:19:28,890
 One object only. Very large. Heading straight for us.

245
00:19:29,930 --> 00:19:33,420
 Single object? What is this? Now what's going on?

246
00:19:33,870 --> 00:19:35,010
 Maximum blow-up on the screen.

247
00:19:37,990 --> 00:19:41,970
 Fleet of Omega, we are here to help you.

248
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,720
 Do not carry out your plans.

249
00:19:45,250 --> 00:19:46,650
 Do not approach Howard Star.

250
00:19:47,310 --> 00:19:48,510
 Let your enemies go there.

251
00:19:49,230 --> 00:19:50,770
 You will take another direction.

252
00:19:51,610 --> 00:19:54,770
 Galactic space towards Star NXSA, second planet.

253
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:56,060
 We will find you there.

254
00:19:56,620 --> 00:19:57,850
 Who are you?

255
00:19:58,310 --> 00:20:00,510
 You can hope for no success in your combat.

256
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:01,690
 Follow our instructions.

257
00:20:02,170 --> 00:20:03,590
 We are your friends, your allies.

258
00:20:03,830 --> 00:20:05,490
 There, you see, didn't I tell you?

259
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:06,950
 They're our allies.

260
00:20:07,870 --> 00:20:11,120
 Come on, Pierre, you can't refuse to follow their instructions.

261
00:20:11,220 --> 00:20:14,760
 I entreat you, do as they have requested.

262
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:16,500
 There is not one minute to lose.

263
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:18,400
 Colonel, I sense your hesitation.

264
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:20,760
 In the name of the trust you have shown in me,

265
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:24,200
 I do sincerely implore you to do exactly what they request.

266
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:27,080
 The fate of the universe is now in your hands, Colonel Pierre.

267
00:20:28,170 --> 00:20:31,460
 This is Colonel Pierre.

268
00:20:32,070 --> 00:20:33,350
 Orders to the entire fleet.

269
00:20:33,850 --> 00:20:36,830
 Direction, galactic space, NXSA, second planet.

270
00:20:37,410 --> 00:20:37,850
 Immediately.

271
00:21:21,980 --> 00:21:51,800
 Leave this.

272
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:52,700
 Swept away.

273
00:21:53,190 --> 00:21:53,590
 Everything.

274
00:21:53,810 --> 00:21:54,810
 Was it a supernova?

275
00:21:55,230 --> 00:21:56,150
 Black hole?

276
00:21:57,040 --> 00:22:00,460
 You see, Pierre, that's what I meant when I tried to convince you

277
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:01,920
 that there are in the cosmos forces

278
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,220
 and dreamed of in our philosophies.

279
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:05,280
 I had poor knowledge of this.

280
00:22:05,830 --> 00:22:07,450
 I knew he spoke the truth.

281
00:22:13,770 --> 00:22:16,760
 Colonel Pierre, to all units,

282
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:19,280
 we are approaching our meeting point.

283
00:22:22,670 --> 00:22:27,080
 We have kept our promise.

284
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:29,820
 Now it is for you to fulfill your promise.

285
00:22:30,430 --> 00:22:31,850
 What are we to do?

286
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:33,510
 Tell us, we're listening.

287
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:36,910
 Let those who best represent you come to us.

288
00:22:37,990 --> 00:22:39,100
 We are waiting.

289
00:22:40,080 --> 00:22:42,740
 Commander, you will ready a shuttle vehicle

290
00:22:42,740 --> 00:22:43,820
 and form a delegation.

291
00:22:44,510 --> 00:22:45,530
 Here we will do the same.

292
00:22:46,760 --> 00:22:48,100
 Carrying out order.

293
00:22:48,810 --> 00:22:50,170
 Hummingbird one, Bluebird,

294
00:22:50,680 --> 00:22:52,320
 escort mission to friendly craft.

295
00:23:53,910 --> 00:24:00,310
 Now, now, they're history.

296
00:24:02,420 --> 00:24:04,730
 A few thousand years.

297
00:24:04,930 --> 00:24:05,960
 They're as children.

298
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:08,020
 Let us allow them this.

299
00:24:08,140 --> 00:24:09,020
 Very well, silent.

300
00:24:09,670 --> 00:24:11,490
 As you requested, we are here.

301
00:24:11,850 --> 00:24:13,100
 Will you now tell us your will?

302
00:24:13,360 --> 00:24:16,980
 In the beginning, the very beginning, man was pure spirit.

303
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:24,780
 He could not bear such infinite timelessness and took on physical form, which in time became human, became you.

304
00:24:25,870 --> 00:24:27,350
 You must now complete the circle.

305
00:24:28,110 --> 00:24:29,510
 Become again what you were.

306
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:31,050
 How are we to do that?

307
00:24:31,320 --> 00:24:31,980
 Tell us.

308
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:36,320
 In your present beings, you are no more than superficially human.

309
00:24:37,020 --> 00:24:39,720
 Only those who have conquered their bodily appetites.

310
00:24:40,040 --> 00:24:41,660
 Only those who truly respect others.

311
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:43,680
 All others, irrespective of difference.

312
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:46,820
 Only they are deep in your conscience.

313
00:24:47,130 --> 00:24:49,500
 Until it can encompass all creatures, all things.

314
00:24:49,520 --> 00:24:50,640
 We struggle in darkness.

315
00:24:50,940 --> 00:24:51,900
 Come, bring us your light.

316
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:52,460
 No.

317
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:56,830
 You will organize your lives and your communities according to your own conscience.

318
00:24:57,450 --> 00:25:00,320
 How are you to find your own way if we take you by the hand?

319
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:02,040
 Is that considerate?

320
00:25:02,040 --> 00:25:05,760
 You can spare us so many painful errors, so much pain, and you refuse?

321
00:25:06,020 --> 00:25:07,720
 Your destiny is your own.

322
00:25:09,450 --> 00:25:13,100
 Truth has meaning only when it is grasped, not when it is given.

323
00:25:13,910 --> 00:25:15,470
 You must travel your own road.

324
00:25:16,170 --> 00:25:17,990
 And how much time do we have for that?

325
00:25:18,260 --> 00:25:19,310
 Time has no meaning.

326
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:25,360
 It is because we have endless time that we have abandoned all ambition, all desire to impose our will.

327
00:25:25,630 --> 00:25:27,560
 Then why did you come to our assistance?

328
00:25:28,290 --> 00:25:35,120
 The cosmos is one coherent whole, with an intelligence even as the tiniest anthill or the human body.

329
00:25:35,120 --> 00:25:38,440
 Those whom we destroyed threatened that natural order.

330
00:25:39,020 --> 00:25:42,140
 We did no more than assist forces already in motion, already present.

331
00:25:42,530 --> 00:25:45,530
 And you must know there is a great deal of good in all of you.

332
00:25:45,930 --> 00:25:46,310
 Go forward.

333
00:25:46,900 --> 00:25:50,310
 On the path toward generosity, understanding, brotherhood.

334
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:52,400
 Seek the shores of the Sea of Tranquility.

335
00:25:52,900 --> 00:25:57,170
 And when you are at the shore of this sea, we will be there to welcome you among us.

336
00:25:58,330 --> 00:25:59,090
 Very well.

337
00:25:59,760 --> 00:26:01,250
 Then we will meet again?

338
00:26:01,730 --> 00:26:02,110
 Yes.

339
00:26:02,660 --> 00:26:05,120
 When the centuries are sufficient for your perfection.

340
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:10,220
 Pyrrho, that's the same thing we said when we were leaving the Cro-Magnon so long ago.

341
00:26:30,790 --> 00:26:32,200
 It's a wonder.

342
00:26:36,410 --> 00:26:40,380
 Come take your place

